g-reference-138","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#createagentconfig","content":"{ budgetTokens } | false"},"141":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-139","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#createagentconfig","content":"off"},"142":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-140","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#createagentconfig","content":"Extended thinking on every run (Anthropic; other providers ignore it). false turns reasoning off on models that reason by default (Nemotron on Nebius, NVIDIA and Ollama), for far fewer output tokens. Reasoning streams as thinking:* events; signed thinking is sent back with tool calls. RunOptions.thinking overrides (false turns it off)"},"143":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-141","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#createagentconfig","content":"logging"},"144":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-142","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#createagentconfig","content":"{ level?, otel?, destination? }"},"145":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-143","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#createagentconfig","content":"'info'"},"146":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-144","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#createagentconfig","content":"Emits log events; otel is shorthand for telemetry: { sink: 'stdout' }"},"147":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-145","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#createagentconfig","content":"telemetry"},"148":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-146","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#createagentconfig","content":"{ endpoint?, apiKey?, sink?, onSpans?, service?, project?, env?, sample?, spans?, toolArgs?, payloads?, memory?, redact?, approvals?, headers? }"},"149":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-147","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#createagentconfig","content":"off (nothing exported)"},"150":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-148","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#createagentconfig","content":"Opt-in observability. With the block present the agent exports agent-shaped spans (LLM calls with tokens and cost, tools, MCP, subagents, workflow steps, approvals, memory, RAG, compaction) to a collector such as @agentkit/telemetry. apiKey (default AGENTKIT_TELEMETRY_KEY) is the tenant's ak_… ingest key; project (default AGENTKIT_TELEMETRY_PROJECT or default) files the spans under a project in that tenant. Every content category (toolArgs, payloads, memory) is off by default; payloads: \"errors\" exports bodies only for a trace that failed; redact names keys dropped before export; onSpans(batch) taps every exported batch (alongside the sink, or on its own when no sink or endpoint is set). Spans go to endpoint, else AGENTKIT_TELEMETRY_URL; with neither (and no sink) they go nowhere but onSpans, so the block can stay in code that only reports where the variable is set. sink: \"stdout\" writes JSON lines instead. Remove the block and nothing is sent"},"151":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-149","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#createagentconfig","content":"harness"},"152":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-150","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#createagentconfig","content":"{ enabled?, record? }"},"153":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-151","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/config-reference#createagentconfig","content":"off"},"154":{"id":"/docs/config-reference-152","page_id":"/docs/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text"