:"/docs/getting-started#presets","content":"For UI, CLI, or backend jobs, start from a preset instead of an empty config:"},"422":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-18","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#presets","content":"See Configuration reference for createCLIPreset and createBackendPreset."},"423":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-19","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#browser-ui","content":"Run the agent on the server, connect from the browser:"},"424":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-20","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#browser-ui","content":"See Streaming & wire protocol for connect(), SSE events, and vanilla JS."},"425":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-21","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#example","content":"See examples/node-backend. Run with mock provider:"},"426":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"Introduction","breadcrumbs":["Documentation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"427":{"id":"/docs-0","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"AgentKit headless agent runtime"},"428":{"id":"/docs-1","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#install","content":"Install"},"429":{"id":"/docs-2","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#two-levels","content":"Two levels"},"430":{"id":"/docs-3","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"431":{"id":"/docs-4","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"AgentKit is a headless agent runtime you import into existing projects, in TypeScript, Python, Go and Rust. Each language runs the whole engine in-process (providers, tools, MCP, memory, RAG, workflows, telemetry, the workspace tools, the server and the client), and any UI connects over the AG-UI wire."},"432":{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"Language"},"433":{"id":"/docs-6","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"Package"},"434":{"id":"/docs-7","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"Install"},"435":{"id":"/docs-8","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"Docs"},"436":{"id":"/docs-9","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"TypeScript (Node 20+)"},"437":{"id":"/docs-10","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"@agentkit/core, @agentkit/server, @agentkit/client"},"438":{"id":"/docs-11","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"pnpm add @agentkit/core @agentkit/server @agentkit/client"},"439":{"id":"/docs-12","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"Getting started"},"440":{"id":"/docs-13","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"Python (3.12+)"},"441":{"id":"/docs-14","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"headless-agentkit, imported as agentkit"},"442":{"id":"/docs-15","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"uv add headless-agentkit"},"443":{"id":"/docs-16","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"Python"},"444":{"id":"/docs-17","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"Go (1.25+)"},"445":{"id":"/docs-18","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"github.com/AbyAbyss/agentkit/sdks/go"},"446":{"id":"/docs-19","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"go get github.com/AbyAbyss/agentkit/sdks/go@latest"},"447":{"id":"/docs-20","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"Go"},"448":{"id":"/docs-21","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"Rust (1.88+)"},"449":{"id":"/docs-22","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"headless-agentkit, imported as agentkit"},"450":{"id":"/docs-23","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"cargo add headless-agentkit"},"451":{"id":"/docs-24","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"Rust"},"452":{"id":"/docs-25","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"TypeScript is the reference engine; the Python, Go and Rust engines are ports checked against it. All four replay the same conformance fixtures, and each of the four clients passes the same contract suite against each of the four servers, so a client in one language can drive a server in another. Each language has an LLM guide for coding agents: LLM_GUIDE.md, LLM_GUIDE.python.md, LLM_GUIDE.go.md and LLM_GUIDE.rust.md."},"453":{"id":"/docs-26","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"The rest of this site shows TypeScript; the Python, Go and Rust sections cover what differs in each."},"454":{"id":"/docs-27","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#install","content":"From this monorepo:"},"455":{"id":"/docs-28","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#two-levels","content":"createAgent(config) is the one-call path, and it covers most projects. Underneath it is a plugin kernel, and the same import gives you that too — services you can replace, extension points you can intercept, and a composition you can publish. That is what you reach for when you are building a coding agent or a domain harness rather than calling a model."},"456":{"id":"/docs-29","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#two-levels","content":"See Extending AgentKit."},"457":{"id":"/docs-30","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#next-steps","content":"Getting started"},"458":{"id":"/docs-31","page_id":"/do