ent":"Sizes"},"1025":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-90","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"Nebius Token Factory"},"1026":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-91","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"\"nebius\""},"1027":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-92","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"NEBIUS_API_KEY"},"1028":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-93","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"nano, super, ultra"},"1029":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-94","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"NVIDIA API catalog (build.nvidia.com)"},"1030":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-95","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"\"nvidia\""},"1031":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-96","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"NVIDIA_API_KEY"},"1032":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-97","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"nano, super, ultra"},"1033":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-98","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"Your own NIM"},"1034":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-99","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"\"nvidia\" + NVIDIA_BASE_URL"},"1035":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-100","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"as your NIM needs"},"1036":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-101","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"what you deploy"},"1037":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-102","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"Ollama (local)"},"1038":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-103","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"\"ollama\""},"1039":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-104","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"none"},"1040":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-105","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"nano, super"},"1041":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-106","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"nemotron(size, host) returns the provider/model id, so the host is one word in config:"},"1042":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-107","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"Ids work with or without the provider prefix: on \"nvidia\", \"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b\" and nemotron(\"ultra\", \"nvidia\") name the same model."},"1043":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-108","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"Reasoning. Nemotron reasons before it answers, which can multiply output tokens (a one-line answer from Nano took 3,703 tokens with reasoning, 117 without). thinking: false in createAgent, or per run (session.send(input, { thinking: false })), turns it off on Nebius, NVIDIA and Ollama."},"1044":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-109","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"Cost. Each size is priced at its own Nebius list price (per million tokens: Ultra $1 in / $3 out, Super $0.30 / $0.90, Nano $0.06 / $0.24), so the console's cost is per model. The \"nvidia\" provider counts $0, since the hosted catalog runs on free credits and a NIM is your own hardware; pass inputCostPerToken / outputCostPerToken to createNvidiaProvider, or call registerModelPrice, to track a paid deployment."},"1045":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-110","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#nemotron-on-any-host","content":"The ids live in NEMOTRON_MODELS. Any other OpenAI-compatible host that serves Nemotron (OpenRouter, vLLM, your gateway) works through registerProvider as shown below. createNvidiaProvider({ apiKey?, baseURL? }) builds the NVIDIA provider directly."},"1046":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-111","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#openai-compatible-gateways","content":"For Azure, LiteLLM, vLLM, or any OpenAI-style /chat/completions API:"},"1047":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-112","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#openai-compatible-gateways","content":"createOpenAICompatibleProvider({ baseURL, apiKey?, id?, inputCostPerToken?, outputCostPerToken? }) returns a Provider suitable for registerProvider."},"1048":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-113","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#session-model-api-agentmodels","content":"When userConfigurable: true (or for registry-only operations), wire clients and React hooks can manage models:"},"1049":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-114","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#session-model-api-agentmodels","content":"Events: models:changed, models:test:result, models:usage:update. Custom provider factories beyond anthropic/openai/ollama/mock require registerProvider (advanced)."},"1050":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-115","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#session-model-api-agentmodels","content":"A single run can use another model without changing the default: session.send(input, { model: \"fast\" }) takes a registry id or a provider/model id."},"1051":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-116","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#picking-a-provider-from-the-environment","content":"detectProviders(env = process.env) returns every built-in provider whose API key is set, in priority order (Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, Mistral, Groq, Nebius, NVIDIA), as { id, provider, model, apiKey } with the provider's default model:"},"1052":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-117","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#offline-rule-based-model-createruleprovider","content":"For demos and tests that should react to what the user types (unlike a fixed __test.mockScript). Each rule matches the latest user message (regex) or a predicate over the conversation, and replies with text, thinking, toolCalls, or a function of the context returning any of those. A tool-call reply whose tools already returned this turn is skipped, so \"call the tool\" followed by \"answer from its result\" sequences a turn; repeat: true on a rule plays it anyway (polling, the same tool with new arguments). fallback answers when nothing matches, and usage fixes the reported usage (a reply may set its own)."},"1053":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-118","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#offline-rule-based-model-createruleprovider","content":"The context a rule sees: messages, lastUser (context a runtime injects mid-turn is not counted as the user), toolResults (this turn), results (the same, decoded: { name, value } with JSON parsed and compacted results unwrapped), tools (names offered), system, and match (the regex result)."},"1054":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-119","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#related","content":"Models & switching — Pattern E, wire parity, presets, extension levels"},"1055":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-120","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#related","content":"Configuration reference — full createAgent table and model routes"},"1056":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-121","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#related","content":"Logging & observability — cost:update per model"},"1057":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-122","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#related","content":"examples/ollama-local — local Ollama agent with /models routes"},"1058":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/providers-123","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/providers#related","content":"examples/node-backend — headless agent.run() with a single provider"},"1059":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/sources","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/sources","type":"page","content":"Sources","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Capabilities"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/capabilities/sources"},"1060":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/sources-0","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/sources","content":"Read-only MCP context in the prompt"},"1061":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/sources-1","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/capabilities/sources#classification","content":"Classification"},"1062":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/sources-2","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/capabilities/sources#prompt-shape","content":"Prompt shape"},"1063":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/sources-3","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/capabilities/sources#task-aware-tool-list","content":"Task-aware tool list"},"1064":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/sources-4","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/capabilities/sources#related","content":"Related"},"1065":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/sources-5","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/sources","content":"Sources are read-only inputs: MCP resources and MCP tools explicitly classified as source (by kind or a classify override). Every other MCP tool, including read-named ones like list_*, get_* or fetch_*, reaches the model as a callable tool. They are encoded with @agentkit/encoding and injected into the system context block — not exposed as callable write tools."},"1066":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/sources-6","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/sources","content":"Use sources when the model should see data (docs, schemas, file trees) without granting a tool that mutates state."},"1067":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/sources-7","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/sources#classification","content":"At init, resources are loaded → buildSourceSnapshots → mcp.refreshSources. The UI receives sources:changed with { sources: [{ id, name }] }."},"1068":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/sources-8","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/sources#prompt-shape","content":"The runtime prepends a block like:"},"1069":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/sources-9","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/sources#prompt-shape","content":"Encoding format follows Context & encoding (context.encoding, default auto)."},"1070":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/sources-10","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/sources#task-aware-tool-list","content":"Callable MCP tools are filtered by getToolsForTask(task) (keyword match on name/description). Sources never appear in that list."},"1071":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/sources-11","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/sources#related","content":"MCP — transports and agent.mcp.resources()"},"1072":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/sources-12","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/sources#related","content":"Context & encoding — TOON vs JSON token savings"},"1073":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/sources-13","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/sources#related","content":"showcase — set kind: \"source\" on mock tools to populate the sources panel"},"1074":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","type":"page","content":"Tools","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Capabilities"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/capabilities/tools"},"1075":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/tools-0","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/tools","content":"Developer-defined Zod tools merged with MCP"},"1076":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/tools-1","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/capabilities/tools#define-a-tool","content":"Define a tool"},"1077":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/tools-2","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/capabilities/tools#report-a-failure-without-throwing","content":"Report a failure without throwing"},"1078":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/tools-3","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/capabilities/tools#many-tools","content":"Many tools"},"1079":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/tools-4","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/capabilities/tools#structured-output","content":"Structured output"},"1080":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/tools-5","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/capabilities/tools#related","content":"Related"},"1081":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/tools-6","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/tools","content":"tools is an array of ToolDef objects: typed inputs (Zod), descriptions for the model, and execute handlers. At runtime they are normalized and merged with MCP tools that are classified as callable (not sources)."},"1082":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/tools-7","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/tools","content":"Define tools when you own the business logic (deploy, query DB, call internal APIs). Prefer MCP when a standard server already exists."},"1083":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/tools-8","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/tools#define-a-tool","content":"Tool lifecycle events: tool:call, tool:result, tool:error. MCP tools use the mcp:tool:* variants when invoked via the MCP manager."},"1084":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/tools-9","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/tools#report-a-failure-without-throwing","content":"Throwing from execute fails the call, and the model gets the error message. When the model\nshould still see the whole result (a command's exit code and output, a partial response),\nreturn it with isError: true and an optional error. The model gets the full result, and the\ncall is recorded as failed: a red tool span with that error in traces, counted in the trace's\n\"N failed calls\" badge and found by the has:error filter."},"1085":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/tools-10","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/tools#report-a-failure-without-throwing","content":"The workspace run_command tool does this for a non-zero exit."},"1086":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/tools-11","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/tools#many-tools","content":"With more than 30 tools, or about 10k tokens of definitions, tool search turns on: each model\ncall gets the likely tools, the rest are listed by group, and a search_tools tool loads more.\nSee Context: tool search."},"1087":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/tools-12","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/tools#structured-output","content":"Pass a Zod schema on run() to constrain the final assistant message:"},"1088":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/tools-13","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/tools#related","content":"Approvals — gate deploy and other write tools"},"1089":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/tools-14","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/tools#related","content":"MCP — external tools namespaced as server__tool"},"1090":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/tools-15","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/tools#related","content":"Static workflows — call tools by name in DAG steps"},"1091":{"id":"/docs/capabilities/tools-16","page_id":"/docs/capabilities/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/capabilities/tools#related","content":"examples/workflow-demo — fetch_issues tool in a workflow"},"1092":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","type":"page","content":"Building a coding agent","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Extending"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent"},"1093":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-0","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","content":"What the spine gives a Claude Code or Codex-style product, what stays yours, and what is still missing"},"1094":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-1","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#the-shape-of-the-product","content":"The shape of the product"},"1095":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-2","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#what-the-spine-already-provides","content":"What the spine already provides"},"1096":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-3","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#what-stays-in-your-product-layer","content":"What stays in your product layer"},"1097":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-4","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#what-is-still-missing","content":"What is still missing"},"1098":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-5","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#a-minimal-v1","content":"A minimal v1"},"1099":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-6","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#related","content":"Related"},"1100":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-7","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","content":"Scope. What AgentKit gives you for a Claude Code or Codex-style product, what it deliberately leaves to you, and what is still missing. Not an IDE: you bring the terminal, web or desktop shell, AgentKit stays the headless engine.Audience. Teams building on @agentkit/core. Verified against the code on main, September 2026."},"1101":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-8","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#the-shape-of-the-product","content":"A multi-session coding agent runs in a terminal, a desktop shell or a web chat without owning an editor. It keeps many conversations, each with its own history and workspace; reads, edits, greps and runs commands in a project root behind approvals and a sandbox; delegates to subagents; persists sessions across restarts and reconnects clients to work in flight."},"1102":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-9","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#the-shape-of-the-product","content":"AgentKit is built for that shape at the plugin level, not the config level. createAgent and @agentkit/workspace still work for the simple case, but a product like this is a harness, and the spine is where a harness lives: createRuntime, agentRuntime(), and plugins on public extension points. Two examples prove it and are the right starting points:"},"1103":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-10","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#the-shape-of-the-product","content":"examples/mini-harness: a terminal coding agent with workspace tools, permissions, plan mode, compaction and a transcript UI, built from public APIs only."},"1104":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-11","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#the-shape-of-the-product","content":"examples/grand-tour: every battery mounted together, twenty-two verified stops, a live dashboard."},"1105":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-12","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#what-the-spine-already-provides","content":"Treat these as done. Each is an ordinary plugin or service; none patches the loop."},"1106":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-13","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#what-the-spine-already-provides","content":"Need"},"1107":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-14","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#what-the-spine-already-provides","content":"Have"},"1108":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-15","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#what-the-spine-already-provides","content":"Where"},"1109":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-16","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#what-the-spine-already-provides","content":"Sessions: list, resume, fork, delete"},"1110":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-17","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent#what-the-spine-already-provides","content":"The append-only session log with a seq on every event"},"1111":{"id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent-18","page_id":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/building-a-coding-