mounts first so it observes every tools/ask before the approver answers, and hooks mounts before approvalPolicy so a hook can veto a call before anyone is asked."},"1546":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-104","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#what-a-stop-looks-like","content":"The hook itself is one line of config in the bundle: a PreToolUse shell command that reads the call on stdin and exits non-zero to refuse it."},"1547":{"id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour-105","page_id":"/docs/extend/grand-tour","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/grand-tour#in-live-mode","content":"--live sends the same prompts to a real provider. The checks then describe what the model did rather than what it had to do; a capable model passes most of them, and a check that fails there is a model choice, not a harness defect."},"1548":{"id":"/docs/extend","page_id":"/docs/extend","type":"page","content":"Extending AgentKit","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Extending"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend"},"1549":{"id":"/docs/extend-0","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend","content":"Two levels, one runtime — from a one-call agent to your own harness"},"1550":{"id":"/docs/extend-1","page_id":"/docs/extend","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend#two-levels","content":"Two levels"},"1551":{"id":"/docs/extend-2","page_id":"/docs/extend","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend#why-a-kernel","content":"Why a kernel"},"1552":{"id":"/docs/extend-3","page_id":"/docs/extend","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend#where-to-reach","content":"Where to reach"},"1553":{"id":"/docs/extend-4","page_id":"/docs/extend","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend#packages","content":"Packages"},"1554":{"id":"/docs/extend-5","page_id":"/docs/extend","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"1555":{"id":"/docs/extend-6","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend","content":"createAgent is the one-call path: configuration goes in, an agent comes out. It covers the common case, and most projects never need anything else."},"1556":{"id":"/docs/extend-7","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend","content":"Underneath it is a plugin kernel, and the same import gives you that too. That is the difference between an SDK you configure and an SDK you build on — the second one lets you ship a coding agent, a review bot, or a domain harness without waiting for AgentKit to add a config key for it."},"1557":{"id":"/docs/extend-8","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#two-levels","content":"Both levels run the same services, the same tool pipeline, and the same session log. Level 2 is not a rewrite of level 1 — it is level 1 with the lid off."},"1558":{"id":"/docs/extend-9","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#why-a-kernel","content":"The old extension surface was a config schema, and a config schema can only express features its author already imagined. Denying a tool call, wrapping a dispatch with a deadline, rewriting what the model sees, or pointing the filesystem at a remote sandbox each meant patching the runtime."},"1559":{"id":"/docs/extend-10","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#why-a-kernel","content":"Now every part of a turn is a service (something you can replace) or an event (something you can intercept). A plugin can deny a tool call, wrap the dispatch, rewrite the prompt, swap the model adapter, add a durable event type, give one session a different tool set, or replace the loop itself — all through public APIs, none of them requiring a change to AgentKit."},"1560":{"id":"/docs/extend-11","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#why-a-kernel","content":"That is also the honesty test: AgentKit's own batteries — skills, retrieval, MCP, recall, budgets, structured output, subagents, session persistence, Code Mode — ship as plugins on this spine. Anything AgentKit does, a third party can do too."},"1561":{"id":"/docs/extend-12","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#where-to-reach","content":"I want to…"},"1562":{"id":"/docs/extend-13","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#where-to-reach","content":"Mechanism"},"1563":{"id":"/docs/extend-14","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#where-to-reach","content":"add a capability"},"1564":{"id":"/docs/extend-15","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#where-to-reach","content":"ctx.tools.register(defineHarnessTool({ … }))"},"1565":{"id":"/docs/extend-16","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#where-to-reach","content":"move every file and shell tool into a sandbox"},"1566":{"id":"/docs/extend-17","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#where-to-reach","content":"swap the ctx.fs + ctx.subprocess providers"},"1567":{"id":"/docs/extend-18","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#where-to-reach","content":"confine paths, or go read-only"},"1568":{"id":"/docs/extend-19","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#where-to-reach","content":"an fs/access listener"},"1569":{"id":"/docs/extend-20","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#where-to-reach","content":"let the model script several tool calls in one step"},"1570":{"id":"/docs/extend-21","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#where-to-reach","content":"mount codeMode"},"1571":{"id":"/docs/extend-22","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#where-to-reach","content":"allow / deny / ask on a tool call"},"1572":{"id":"/docs/extend-23","page_id":"/docs/extend","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend#where-to-r