-smoke-test","content":"Every other test in this repo runs against a scripted adapter. Those verify the runtime, but they cannot tell you whether a real provider accepts the request or whether a real model can actually drive the tools."},"1760":{"id":"/docs/extend/mini-harness-55","page_id":"/docs/extend/mini-harness","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/mini-harness#the-live-smoke-test","content":"It makes real requests against a temporary workspace and checks five things a mock cannot: that a model picks a tool and uses its result, that it produces arguments the schema accepts and the write lands on disk, that a command round-trips through the subprocess seam, that the log records every model-visible fact, and that history derived from the log alone reproduces the conversation."},"1761":{"id":"/docs/extend/mini-harness-56","page_id":"/docs/extend/mini-harness","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/mini-harness#the-live-smoke-test","content":"It costs money, which is why it is a script rather than part of pnpm test. Without a key it exits with a message instead of failing."},"1762":{"id":"/docs/extend/mini-harness-57","page_id":"/docs/extend/mini-harness","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/mini-harness#next","content":"Extending AgentKit — the mechanism table, if you arrived here first"},"1763":{"id":"/docs/extend/mini-harness-58","page_id":"/docs/extend/mini-harness","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/mini-harness#next","content":"Bundles — how to publish a harness others can retune"},"1764":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","type":"page","content":"Agent runtime","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Extending"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/runtime"},"1765":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-0","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime","content":"Services, the anatomy of a turn, and every extension point"},"1766":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-1","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtim