e_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#extension-points","content":"answer a permission question"},"1836":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-71","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#extension-points","content":"fs/access"},"1837":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-72","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#extension-points","content":"waterfall"},"1838":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-73","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#extension-points","content":"confine paths, or go read-only"},"1839":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-74","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#extension-points","content":"subprocess/spawn"},"1840":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-75","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#extension-points","content":"waterfall"},"1841":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-76","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#extension-points","content":"vet or rewrite a command"},"1842":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-77","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#extension-points","content":"session/event"},"1843":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-78","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#extension-points","content":"emit"},"1844":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-79","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#extension-points","content":"render a UI, ship telemetry, persist"},"1845":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-80","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#extension-points","content":"Plus ctx.tools.guard() for a monotonic deny no listener can talk past, and ctx.tools.restrict() for a visible set that presentation, lookup, and execution all read through."},"1846":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-81","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#a-policy-plugin-end-to-end","content":"A decision is { kind: \"allow\" }, { kind: \"deny\", reason }, or { kind: \"ask\", question }. The runtime — not your plugin — runs the tools/ask serial when a listener answers ask, so asking and answering stay independently replaceable."},"1847":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-82","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#a-policy-plugin-end-to-end","content":"The difference between the two mechanisms matters. A tools/pre-execute listener is policy — reorderable, overridable, and the right home for \"ask the user\". A guard is an invariant — it only ever adds refusals, and a derived registry inherits it, so moving into a realm cannot escape it."},"1848":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-83","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#a-policy-plugin-end-to-end","content":"exec carries name, frozen arguments, sessionId, an AbortSignal, and inject(content) for pushing model-visible context into the next request."},"1849":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-84","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#prompt-assembly","content":"Sections are ordered and independently owned, so two plugins can each contribute context without knowing about each other:"},"1850":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-85","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#prompt-assembly","content":"Lower order runs first, and the convention leaves gaps: 10 identity, 20 policy, 40 context, 80 skills. The id is stable, so a later plugin can shadow a section by reusing it. ctx.systemPrompt.list() shows what would render, in order."},"1851":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-86","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#prompt-assembly","content":"system-prompt/assemble is the waterfall around the finished prompt, for anyone who needs the last word."},"1852":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-87","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#replacing-the-loop","content":"Everything else — tools, prompt, log, agents — keeps working, because none of them call the loop; the loop calls them."},"1853":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-88","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#optional-plugins","content":"agentRuntime() deliberately mounts only the spine. These ship alongside it and are opt-in, because each one is a policy choice rather than a default:"},"1854":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-89","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#optional-plugins","content":"budget enforces cost, token, tool-call, step, and duration ceilings per session. It is pure bookkeeping over session/event plus two refusals — agent/pre-step for the next step, tools/pre-execute for a call inside a step already underway — so nothing in the loop knows a budget exists. A breach refuses the next step rather than aborting mid-flight, so the log ends on a clean turn boundary."},"1855":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-90","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#optional-plugins","content":"structuredOutput requires a session's final answer to match a schema:"},"1856":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-91","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#optional-plugins","content":"It adds the requirement to the prompt, validates on agent/turn-stopping, feeds a failed parse back as one more step, and appends the accepted value as a durable structured/output event. A fenced block or surrounding prose is tolerated; anything past the attempt limit is logged as an error rather than looped on."},"1857":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-92","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#optional-plugins","content":"Subagents are three separate plugins on purpose: subagentsPlugin is the registry, inProcessSubagents is one provider, and subagentTool is the model-facing task tool. Swapping the provider for a forked process or a remote runtime changes nothing else. A definition with tools gets its own realm via ctx.isolate(\"tools\"), so a restricted subagent genuinely cannot reach the parent's other tools, and its identity is a scoped prompt section rather than a user message it could be argued out of."},"1858":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-93","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#persistence","content":"@agentkit/runtime ships only MemorySessionStore so it stays edge-capable. The Node-side implementations of the same seam live in @agentkit/core:"},"1859":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-94","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#persistence","content":"Scoped like any other registration: unloading the plugin puts the in-memory store back rather than leaving the runtime pointed at a closed handle."},"1860":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-95","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#next","content":"Session log — the projection rule everything else rests on"},"1861":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-96","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#next","content":"Tool contract — one definition, four consumers"},"1862":{"id":"/docs/extend/runtime-97","page_id":"/docs/extend/runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/runtime#next","content":"Execution seams — where file and process access actually happens"},"1863":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","type":"page","content":"Session log","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Extending"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/sessions"},"1864":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-0","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/sessions","content":"Model-visible means logged — one mechanism instead of five features"},"1865":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-1","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/sessions#the-invariant","content":"The invariant"},"1866":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-2","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/sessions#adding-a-durable-fact","content":"Adding a durable fact"},"1867":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-3","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/sessions#compaction-without-mutation","content":"Compaction, without mutation"},"1868":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-4","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/sessions#fork-resume-replay","content":"Fork, resume, replay"},"1869":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-5","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/sessions#watching-the-log","content":"Watching the log"},"1870":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-6","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/sessions#swapping-the-store","content":"Swapping the store"},"1871":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-7","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/sessions#next","content":"Next"},"1872":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-8","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/sessions","content":"The session log is an append-only event log, and model history is a projection of it. That is the whole design, and everything else on this page follows from it."},"1873":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-9","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/sessions","content":"deriveMessages() builds the model's view of the conversation from the log, and it is the only supported way to build it. That single rule is what makes fork, resume, replay, durable UI, and telemetry fall out of one mechanism instead of being five separate features."},"1874":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-10","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/sessions#the-invariant","content":"Anything that reaches a model request must be reconstructable from the log."},"1875":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-11","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/sessions#the-invariant","content":"If a plugin sneaks context into a request without logging it, the session can no longer be forked, resumed, or replayed faithfully — and the bug does not show up until someone tries. So the rule is enforced at the seam: the loop derives history from the log, and nowhere else."},"1876":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-12","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/sessions#adding-a-durable-fact","content":"A plugin that needs durable state extends the event map and says how the model should see it:"},"1877":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-13","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/sessions#adding-a-durable-fact","content":"Register no projector and the fact is still durable, still visible to the UI and to telemetry, and simply stays out of the prompt. That is the normal case for metrics and UI state."},"1878":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-14","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/sessions#adding-a-durable-fact","content":"SessionEvent is a discriminated union, so switch (event.type) narrows event.data with no casts."},"1879":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-15","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/sessions#compaction-without-mutation","content":"Compaction works the same way: it appends a context/compacted boundary rather than rewriting history. The projection stays a pure function of the log, so the original events are still there for audit, and a fork taken before the boundary still replays the full conversation."},"1880":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-16","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/sessions#compaction-without-mutation","content":"deriveMessages collapses everything up to the boundary into a single summary turn, so the model sees the compacted view while the log keeps the originals."},"1881":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-17","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/sessions#fork-resume-replay","content":"Resume is not a feature — it is what happens when a persistent store is mounted and the log is read back. Sequence numbers hydrate from the store on the first append, so a resumed session continues its numbering rather than overwriting history."},"1882":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-18","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/sessions#watching-the-log","content":"session/event is emitted for every append. A UI, a telemetry exporter, and a persistence layer are all the same kind of subscriber:"},"1883":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-19","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/sessions#watching-the-log","content":"This is why the transcript UI in mini-harness imports no tool, and gets new tools' cards for free."},"1884":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-20","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/sessions#swapping-the-store","content":"useStore is scoped like any other registration, so unloading the persistence plugin puts the in-memory store back rather than leaving the runtime pointed at a closed handle:"},"1885":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-21","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/sessions#swapping-the-store","content":"kind is \"sqlite\", \"jsonl\", or \"custom\" with your own SessionStore — four methods: append, read, list, drop. @agentkit/runtime alone ships MemorySessionStore so it stays edge-capable."},"1886":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-22","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/sessions#next","content":"Tool contract — what a tool/result event carries, and why"},"1887":{"id":"/docs/extend/sessions-23","page_id":"/docs/extend/sessions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/sessions#next","content":"Agent runtime — where the log sits in a turn"},"1888":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","type":"page","content":"Tool contract","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Extending"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/tools"},"1889":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-0","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools","content":"One definition, four consumers — arguments, canonical value, model prose, and a UI card"},"1890":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-1","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/tools#registration","content":"Registration"},"1891":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-2","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/tools#execution-pipeline","content":"Execution pipeline"},"1892":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-3","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/tools#visibility","content":"Visibility"},"1893":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-4","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/tools#cards","content":"Cards"},"1894":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-5","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/tools#the-exec-handle","content":"The exec handle"},"1895":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-6","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/extend/tools#next","content":"Next"},"1896":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-7","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools","content":"A tool has four audiences and they want different things. The runtime validates arguments, code consumes a canonical value, the model reads prose, and a UI renders a card. Collapsing those into one string is what makes tool output either unusable by code or unreadable by the model."},"1897":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-8","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools","content":"defineHarnessTool keeps them separate in one definition. (It is exported under that name from @agentkit/core so it does not collide with the simpler defineTool used by createAgent; both run on the same pipeline.)"},"1898":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-9","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools","content":"input is validated before execute runs, so args is typed inside with no guard clauses. Without an output.render the value is stringified — fine for simple tools, lossy for everything else."},"1899":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-10","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools","content":"A value that describes a failure — a command's non-zero exit — can still be returned rather than thrown: output.isError(args, value) marks the result isError while the model reads the rendered value as usual. bashTool does this for a non-zero exit, so the session log, UIs, workflows and Code Mode see the command fail."},"1900":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-11","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#registration","content":"Registration is effect-scoped: a tool belongs to the plugin that registered it and disappears when that plugin unloads. There is no global tool table to clean up."},"1901":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-12","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#registration","content":"A tool that already publishes its own model-facing schema — an MCP server, for instance — passes it as jsonSchema and owns its own validation, rather than having one derived from a placeholder Zod type."},"1902":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-13","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#execution-pipeline","content":"Every call runs through four extension points, in order:"},"1903":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-14","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#execution-pipeline","content":"guard() — a monotonic deny no later listener can undo. Invariants."},"1904":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-15","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#execution-pipeline","content":"tools/pre-execute — the reorderable allow / deny / ask policy layer."},"1905":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-16","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#execution-pipeline","content":"tools/execute — wraps the dispatch itself: deadlines, retries, metrics."},"1906":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-17","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#execution-pipeline","content":"tools/post-execute — transforms the result; tools/result observes it."},"1907":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-18","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#execution-pipeline","content":"Execution never throws. A guard that throws, a policy listener that throws, an approval answerer that throws, and execute itself throwing all become an error ToolResult — because a tool failure is a conversation the model can recover from, and an exception out of the pipeline would take the whole turn with it."},"1908":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-19","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#visibility","content":"Presentation, lookup, and execution all read through the filter, so a hidden tool cannot be called by name either. That is what makes a read-only plan mode real rather than advisory."},"1909":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-20","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#visibility","content":"Filters are owned by the registry that declares them; guards are inherited from the parent. So a realm can narrow a subagent's tool set without narrowing anyone else's, and still cannot escape the parent's invariants."},"1910":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-21","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#cards","content":"presentCall and presentResult return a render intent, not markup."},"1911":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-22","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#cards","content":"A pending call renders as generic, terminal, or diff. A completed call adds search and web:"},"1912":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-23","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#cards","content":"card"},"1913":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-24","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#cards","content":"completed shape"},"1914":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-25","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#cards","content":"generic"},"1915":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-26","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#cards","content":"title?, content?"},"1916":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-27","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#cards","content":"terminal"},"1917":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-28","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#cards","content":"output, exitCode?"},"1918":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-29","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#cards","content":"diff"},"1919":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-30","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#cards","content":"diffs: { path, oldText, newText }[]"},"1920":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-31","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#cards","content":"search"},"1921":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-32","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#cards","content":"shape: \"matches\" | \"paths\", results, total?, truncated?"},"1922":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-33","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#cards","content":"web"},"1923":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-34","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#cards","content":"kind: \"search\" | \"fetch\", sources?, summary?"},"1924":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-35","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#cards","content":"The tool never imports a UI type; a host maps each card into its own views. @agentkit/react ships a default mapping."},"1925":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-36","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#cards","content":"Presenters are pure — no I/O, no clock, no session reads — because they run on live streaming and on replay from meta persisted on the tool/result event. A presenter that throws yields no card rather than crashing the replay."},"1926":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-37","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#the-exec-handle","content":"field"},"1927":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-38","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#the-exec-handle","content":"is"},"1928":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-39","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#the-exec-handle","content":"name"},"1929":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-40","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#the-exec-handle","content":"the tool being called"},"1930":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-41","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#the-exec-handle","content":"arguments"},"1931":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-42","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#the-exec-handle","content":"frozen before policy runs; read-only input"},"1932":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-43","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#the-exec-handle","content":"sessionId"},"1933":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-44","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#the-exec-handle","content":"the session this call belongs to"},"1934":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-45","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#the-exec-handle","content":"signal"},"1935":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-46","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#the-exec-handle","content":"cancels this call; a tools/execute wrapper may replace it to impose a deadline, but not remove it"},"1936":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-47","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#the-exec-handle","content":"token"},"1937":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-48","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#the-exec-handle","content":"opaque identity for this dispatch, stable across the whole pipeline"},"1938":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-49","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#the-exec-handle","content":"inject(content, source?)"},"1939":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-50","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#the-exec-handle","content":"append model-visible context the next request will carry"},"1940":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-51","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#next","content":"Code Mode — where the canonical value earns its keep"},"1941":{"id":"/docs/extend/tools-52","page_id":"/docs/extend/tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/extend/tools#next","content":"Execution seams — where a tool's file and process access actually goes"},"1942":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","type":"page","content":"Config in Go","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Go"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/go/config-reference"},"1943":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-0","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference","content":"How createAgent's config, options and results map to the Go port"},"1944":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-1","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/go/config-reference#config-in-go","content":"Config in Go"},"1945":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-2","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"The config is a struct named after TypeScript's keys"},"1946":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-3","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"Go names are exported identifiers"},"1947":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-4","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/go/config-reference#what-is-sent-stored-or-emitted-keeps-typescripts-keys","content":"What is sent, stored or emitted keeps TypeScript's keys"},"1948":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-5","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/go/config-reference#schemas-are-go-types","content":"Schemas are Go types"},"1949":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-6","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/go/config-reference#functions-are-go-functions-and-take-a-context","content":"Functions are Go functions, and take a context"},"1950":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-7","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/go/config-reference#errors-cancellation-and-closing","content":"Errors, cancellation and closing"},"1951":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-8","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/go/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"Where the port differs, and why"},"1952":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-9","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/go/config-reference#feature-status","content":"Feature status"},"1953":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-10","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#config-in-go","content":"The Go port takes the same configuration as TypeScript, as a typed struct instead of an object literal. What changes is the host language around it: names, optional values, schemas, functions and errors. This page lists each mapping and why it is that way."},"1954":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-11","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"agentkit.CreateAgent(config) takes an agentkit.Config (an alias of agent.Config). Each field is the TypeScript key with its first letter capitalised, and nested blocks are their own structs:"},"1955":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-12","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"TypeScript"},"1956":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-13","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"Go"},"1957":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-14","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"provider: \"anthropic\""},"1958":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-15","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"Provider: agentkit.Provider(\"anthropic\")"},"1959":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-16","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"provider: { default, userConfigurable }"},"1960":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-17","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"Provider: providers.ProviderConfig{Default: ..., UserConfigurable: true}"},"1961":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-18","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"system: \"...\" or a function"},"1962":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-19","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"System: agentkit.SystemText(\"...\") or agent.SystemFunc(fn)"},"1963":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-20","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"memory: false"},"1964":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-21","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"Memory: &memory.MemoryConfig{Disabled: true}"},"1965":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-22","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"mcp: false"},"1966":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-23","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"MCP: &agent.MCPConfig{Disabled: true}"},"1967":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-24","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"thinking: false"},"1968":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-25","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"NoThinking: true"},"1969":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-26","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"workspace: { project: false }"},"1970":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-27","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"Workspace: &agent.WorkspaceConfig{NoProject: true}"},"1971":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-28","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"__test: { mockScript }"},"1972":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-29","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"Test: &agent.TestConfig{MockScript: ...}"},"1973":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-30","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"Optional values are pointers where zero is a meaningful setting: CompactAt *float64, Enabled *bool, AutoApproveAfterMs *int. A nil pointer means \"not set, use the default\", so 0 and false stay expressible. Blocks are pointers too; a nil block is TypeScript's omitted key."},"1974":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-31","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"x: false has a name. Go cannot hold false in a struct field, so a block that TypeScript switches off with false has a Disabled field (Memory, MCP, scratch, artifacts) or a No... field (NoThinking, NoProject, NoArtifacts)."},"1975":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-32","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"Validation happens in CreateAgent, with Zod's wording. A bad config returns an error whose message starts Invalid createAgent config: and lists each problem on its TypeScript path (telemetry.sample: Number must be less than or equal to 1); no agent is built."},"1976":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-33","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"Presets (agentkit.CreateUIPreset, CreateCLIPreset, CreateBackendPreset) return an agent.Config; pass overrides as functions: agentkit.CreateBackendPreset(func(c *agentkit.Config) { c.Mode = agentkit.ModePlan }). The coding preset is workspace.CreateCodingAgentPreset, which returns (agent.Config, error)."},"1977":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-34","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"TypeScript"},"1978":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-35","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"Go"},"1979":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-36","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"createAgent(config)"},"1980":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-37","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"agentkit.CreateAgent(config) returning (*Agent, error)"},"1981":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-38","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"await agent.run(task, { output, onApproval })"},"1982":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-39","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"a.Run(ctx, task, agentkit.RunOptions{Output: ..., OnApproval: fn})"},"1983":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-40","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"agent.stream(task)"},"1984":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-41","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"a.Stream(ctx, task)"},"1985":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-42","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"agent.session({ userId, meta })"},"1986":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-43","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"a.Session(agentkit.SessionOptions{UserID: \"u1\", Meta: ...})"},"1987":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-44","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"agent.setMode(\"plan\")"},"1988":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-45","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"a.SetMode(agentkit.ModePlan)"},"1989":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-46","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"agent.models.setDefault(id)"},"1990":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-47","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"a.Models().SetDefault(id)"},"1991":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-48","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"agent.rag, agent.mcp, agent.workflows"},"1992":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-49","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"a.RAG(), a.MCP(), a.Workflows()"},"1993":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-50","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"agent.on(\"stream:token\", fn)"},"1994":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-51","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"agentkit.On(a, types.KeyStreamToken, fn) (typed) or a.On(\"stream:token\", fn)"},"1995":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-52","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"await agent.close()"},"1996":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-53","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"a.Close(ctx)"},"1997":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-54","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#go-names-are-exported-identifiers","content":"RunResult has Output, Usage, Trace, Cost, StepCount, ToolCalls, Artifacts, Handoff and TraceID, with the TypeScript JSON keys as struct tags."},"1998":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-55","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#what-is-sent-stored-or-emitted-keeps-typescripts-keys","content":"Event payloads, wire bodies, recordings, session logs and anything persisted keep TypeScript's shape. In process, events are typed: types.EventKey[P] pairs an event name with its payload struct, so the compiler checks both sides:"},"1999":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-56","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#what-is-sent-stored-or-emitted-keeps-typescripts-keys","content":"Their JSON tags carry the TypeScript keys, which is what lets a TypeScript UI read a Go server and a recording made by one engine replay in another. Over the wire, the Go client hands payloads to handlers as decoded JSON (map[string]any)."},"2000":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-57","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#schemas-are-go-types","content":"Where TypeScript takes a Zod schema, Go takes a type parameter. A tool's arguments are a struct; its JSON Schema is reflected from the fields and their tags (json, description, enum, default), and the model's arguments are validated with Zod's wording before Execute sees them:"},"2001":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-58","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#schemas-are-go-types","content":"Execute receives the decoded struct. A structured Output comes back as a value of the type you named."},"2002":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-59","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#functions-are-go-functions-and-take-a-context","content":"Every function-valued key takes a Go function whose first parameter is a context.Context and whose last result is an error:"},"2003":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-60","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#functions-are-go-functions-and-take-a-context","content":"Key"},"2004":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-61","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#functions-are-go-functions-and-take-a-context","content":"Go"},"2005":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-62","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#functions-are-go-functions-and-take-a-context","content":"system"},"2006":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-63","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#functions-are-go-functions-and-take-a-context","content":"agent.SystemFunc(func(ctx context.Context, pc agent.PromptContext) (string, error)); pc has UserID, OrgID, Meta, Mode, Task"},"2007":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-64","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#functions-are-go-functions-and-take-a-context","content":"hooks.beforeModel, beforeTool, afterTool, onOutput"},"2008":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-65","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#functions-are-go-functions-and-take-a-context","content":"fields of agent.AgentHooks; each returns a result struct (&agent.BeforeToolResult{Block: \"why\"}) or nil for no change"},"2009":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-66","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#functions-are-go-functions-and-take-a-context","content":"approvals.policy"},"2010":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-67","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#functions-are-go-functions-and-take-a-context","content":"func(ctx, tool approvals.PolicyTool, session approvals.PolicySessionContext) (approvals.ToolPolicy, error); return \"\" to fall through"},"2011":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-68","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#functions-are-go-functions-and-take-a-context","content":"onApproval, onElicitation (run or send options)"},"2012":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-69","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#functions-are-go-functions-and-take-a-context","content":"RunOptions.OnApproval, RunOptions.OnElicitation"},"2013":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-70","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#errors-cancellation-and-closing","content":"Errors are returned, not thrown. Where TypeScript throws, Go returns an error. A panic in a tool or an event listener is recovered where TypeScript would catch the throw: the tool's panic becomes a tool error the model reads, the listener's an error event."},"2014":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-71","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#errors-cancellation-and-closing","content":"Cancellation is the context. Cancel the ctx passed to Run or Send where TypeScript passes an AbortSignal; a tool's Execute gets a context that ends with the run or the tool's timeout."},"2015":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-72","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#errors-cancellation-and-closing","content":"Always a.Close(ctx), which disconnects MCP servers and closes memory and cache stores. A client session has Close(), which returns at once (safe inside an event handler), and Shutdown(ctx), which also waits for the event stream's goroutine."},"2016":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-73","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#errors-cancellation-and-closing","content":"Everything is safe for concurrent use: one agent serves many sessions from many goroutines."},"2017":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-74","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"Map keys print sorted. Go maps have no insertion order, so a JSON object built from a map[string]any (a tool's schema properties, a stringified result) lists its keys sorted. Use a struct, or a json.RawMessage, where key order matters."},"2018":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-75","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"JavaScript semantics where they show. String lengths in UTF-16 units, JavaScript's trim() and \\s, Number#toString, toFixed and Math.round are reproduced wherever their result reaches the wire, a prompt or a fixture, so output matches byte for byte."},"2019":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-76","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"Session ownership without AsyncLocalStorage. A session emits through an owned view of the agent's event bus, and each turn carries it in its context, so the server routes subagent, RAG and MCP tool events to the session that raised them. A component that emits on its own should read the bus with events.BusFrom(ctx, fallback)."},"2020":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-77","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"Heavy drivers are opt-in imports, as listed in Getting started."},"2021":{"id":"/docs/go/config-reference-78","page_id":"/docs/go/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"The server is net/http. See One wire, four engines."},"2022":{"id":"/docs