/todo/edit, /workflows*, /mcp* (with the OAuth callback), /rag/*, /models*, /health, /capabilities. With Transport: server.TransportWebSocket, /events is a WebSocket. Auth, tenant isolation (TenantHeader), CORS, Host checks (AllowedHosts, default on a loopback bind), the 4 MiB body limit and the session cap (MaxSessions) are ported from handler.ts."},"2127":{"id":"/docs/go/wire-39","page_id":"/docs/go/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/wire#the-go-server","content":"Each event stream has its own queue and goroutine, so a slow client never blocks the agent, and a session route waits for its streams to flush before it replies: /send cannot answer ahead of its tokens."},"2128":{"id":"/docs/go/wire-40","page_id":"/docs/go/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/wire#the-go-client","content":"Package client talks to any AgentKit server:"},"2129":{"id":"/docs/go/wire-41","page_id":"/docs/go/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/wire#the-go-client","content":"It reconnects dropped streams with backoff, client.ConnectWithRetry waits for a server that is still starting, and client.ConnectAgents(url, opts) talks to ServeAgents. The session hub folds events with the same reducers as the TypeScript client (conversation, pending, todos, usage, workflow), in package client/state."},"2130":{"id":"/docs/go/wire-42","page_id":"/docs/go/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/wire#the-go-client","content":"Two things differ from TypeScript. Handlers for server events run on the stream's reader goroutine, so keep them short or hand work off. And Close() returns at once (a handler may call it) while Shutdown(ctx) also waits for that goroutine. The event stream starts with the first subscriber; wait for session.Status() == client.StatusOpen before a Send whose events you must not miss."},"2131":{"id":"/docs/go/wire-43","page_id":"/docs/go/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/wire#how-the-sameness-is-checked","content":"The client contract, in all sixteen pairings. A contract host in each language (sdks/conformance/contract/ts_host.mjs, python_host.py, the Go one in sdks/go/internal/contracthost and the Rust examples/contract_host.rs) builds an agent from a JSON config and serves it on a free port (POST /serve, /serve-agents, /close). TypeScript's packages/server/src/client-contract.test.ts runs unmodified against any host, and so do its Python, Go and Rust ports:"},"2132":{"id":"/docs/go/wire-44","page_id":"/docs/go/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/wire#how-the-sameness-is-checked","content":"The wire frames, byte for byte. sdks/conformance/fixtures/wire.json holds the AG-UI frames the TypeScript adapter produces for every event name; the Go server replays them exactly. CI regenerates every fixture from the TypeScript source and fails on any difference."},"2133":{"id":"/docs/go/wire-45","page_id":"/docs/go/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/go/wire#how-the-sameness-is-checked","content":"The dashboards, unchanged. Two pages built for the TypeScript server run against the Go one with no edits:"},"2134":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","type":"page","content":"Config in Rust","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Rust"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/rust/config-reference"},"2135":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-0","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference","content":"How createAgent's config, options and results map to the Rust port"},"2136":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-1","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#config-in-rust","content":"Config in Rust"},"2137":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-2","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"The config is a struct named after TypeScript's keys"},"2138":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-3","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"Rust names are snake_case"},"2139":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-4","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#what-is-sent-stored-or-emitted-keeps-typescripts-keys","content":"What is sent, stored or emitted keeps TypeScript's keys"},"2140":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-5","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#schemas-are-rust-types","content":"Schemas are Rust types"},"2141":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-6","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#functions-are-closures-that-return-futures","content":"Functions are closures that return futures"},"2142":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-7","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#errors-cancellation-and-closing","content":"Errors, cancellation and closing"},"2143":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-8","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"Where the port differs, and why"},"2144":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-9","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#feature-status","content":"Feature status"},"2145":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-10","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#config-in-rust","content":"The Rust port takes the same configuration as TypeScript, as a typed struct instead of an object literal. What changes is the host language around it: names, optional values, schemas, functions and errors. This page lists each mapping and why it is that way."},"2146":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-11","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"agentkit::create_agent(config) takes an agentkit::Config. Each field is the TypeScript key in snake_case, nested blocks are their own structs (in agent::config or the module they configure), and every optional field is an Option. Config has no Default, because the provider is required: start from Config::new(provider) and use struct update syntax."},"2147":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-12","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"TypeScript"},"2148":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-13","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"Rust"},"2149":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-14","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"provider: \"anthropic\""},"2150":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-15","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"Config::new(\"anthropic\") (a ProviderConfigInput from a &str)"},"2151":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-16","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"provider: { default, userConfigurable }"},"2152":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-17","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"Config::new(ProviderConfig { default, user_configurable: true, .. })"},"2153":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-18","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"system: \"...\" or a function"},"2154":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-19","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"system: Some(\"...\".into()) or Some(SystemPrompt::Function(..))"},"2155":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-20","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"memory: false"},"2156":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-21","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"memory: Some(MemoryConfig::disabled())"},"2157":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-22","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"mcp: false"},"2158":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-23","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"mcp: Some(OrFalse::Disabled)"},"2159":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-24","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"thinking: false"},"2160":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-25","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"thinking: Some(Thinking::Off)"},"2161":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-26","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"handoff: true"},"2162":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-27","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"handoff: Some(BoolOr::Bool(true))"},"2163":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-28","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"workspace: { project: false }"},"2164":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-29","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"workspace: Some(WorkspaceConfig { project: Some(OrFalse::Disabled), .. })"},"2165":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-30","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"__test: { mockScript }"},"2166":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-31","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"test: Some(TestConfig { mock_script: Some(..), .. })"},"2167":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-32","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"None means \"not set, use the default\", so Some(0) and Some(false) stay expressible: compact_at: Some(0.0), enabled: Some(false). Sub-configs derive Default, so ..XConfig::default() fills the rest."},"2168":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-33","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"x: false has a type. TypeScript's T | false is OrFalse<T> (Disabled or Set(T)), boolean | T is BoolOr<T> (Bool(b) or Value(T)), and a block switched off as a whole has a constructor (MemoryConfig::disabled())."},"2169":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-34","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"Validation happens in create_agent, with Zod's wording. A bad config returns AgentError::Config whose message starts Invalid createAgent config: and lists each problem on its TypeScript path (telemetry.sample: Number must be less than or equal to 1); no agent is built. A TypeScript-shaped JSON config deserialises into Config with serde and gets the same checks."},"2170":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-35","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#the-config-is-a-struct-named-after-typescripts-keys","content":"Presets (create_ui_preset, create_cli_preset, create_backend_preset) return a Config; override with struct update syntax: Config { mode: Some(AgentMode::Plan), ..create_backend_preset() }. The coding preset is create_coding_agent_preset(CodingAgentPresetOptions::new(root, provider)) (feature workspace), which returns Result<Config, _>."},"2171":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-36","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"TypeScript"},"2172":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-37","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"Rust"},"2173":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-38","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"createAgent(config)"},"2174":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-39","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"agentkit::create_agent(config) returning Result<Agent, AgentError>"},"2175":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-40","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"await agent.run(task, { output, onApproval })"},"2176":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-41","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"agent.run(task, RunOptions { output, on_approval, .. }).await"},"2177":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-42","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"agent.stream(task)"},"2178":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-43","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"agent.stream(task, opts), an AgentStream (a futures::Stream of events, then .result().await)"},"2179":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-44","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"agent.session({ userId, meta })"},"2180":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-45","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"agent.session(SessionOptions { user_id, meta, .. })"},"2181":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-46","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"agent.setMode(\"plan\")"},"2182":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-47","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"agent.set_mode(AgentMode::Plan)"},"2183":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-48","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"agent.models.setDefault(id)"},"2184":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-49","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"agent.models().set_default(id)"},"2185":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-50","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"agent.rag, agent.mcp, agent.workflows"},"2186":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-51","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"agent.rag(), agent.mcp(), agent.workflows(), each an Option"},"2187":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-52","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"agent.on(\"stream:token\", fn)"},"2188":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-53","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"agentkit::events::on(agent.bus(), keys::STREAM_TOKEN, fn) (typed) or agent.on(\"stream:token\", fn)"},"2189":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-54","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"await agent.close()"},"2190":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-55","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"agent.close().await"},"2191":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-56","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#rust-names-are-snake_case","content":"RunResult has output (a serde_json::Value), usage, trace, cost, step_count, tool_calls, artifacts, handoff, trace_id and status, with the TypeScript JSON keys through serde."},"2192":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-57","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#what-is-sent-stored-or-emitted-keeps-typescripts-keys","content":"Event payloads, wire bodies, recordings, session logs and anything persisted keep TypeScript's shape. In process, events can be typed: an EventKey<P> in agentkit::types::keys pairs an event name with its payload struct, so the compiler checks both sides."},"2193":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-58","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#what-is-sent-stored-or-emitted-keeps-typescripts-keys","content":"Their serde names carry the TypeScript keys, which is what lets a TypeScript UI read a Rust server and a recording made by one engine replay in another. Over the wire, the Rust client hands payloads to handlers as &serde_json::Value. serde_json is built with preserve_order, so objects keep the key order TypeScript writes."},"2194":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-59","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#schemas-are-rust-types","content":"Where TypeScript takes a Zod schema, Rust takes a type. A tool's arguments are a struct that derives Deserialize, JsonSchema (schemars) and Clone; its JSON Schema comes from the fields, doc comments become descriptions, and the model's arguments are validated with Zod's wording before the body sees them. Refinements are schemars attributes (#[schemars(length(min = 1))], range, url), checked after the type check and stripped from the schema the model sees. An Option<T> field is optional and accepts null."},"2195":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-60","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#schemas-are-rust-types","content":"The body receives the decoded struct and returns any Serialize value. A structured output (RunOptions.output = Some(output_type::<T>())) is validated against T's schema and comes back as JSON in result.output; decode it with serde_json::from_value::<T>."},"2196":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-61","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#functions-are-closures-that-return-futures","content":"Every function-valued key is an Arc<dyn Fn(..) -> BoxFuture<'static, Result<..>>>, so a closure returns Box::pin(async move { .. }):"},"2197":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-62","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#functions-are-closures-that-return-futures","content":"Key"},"2198":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-63","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#functions-are-closures-that-return-futures","content":"Rust"},"2199":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-64","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#functions-are-closures-that-return-futures","content":"system"},"2200":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-65","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#functions-are-closures-that-return-futures","content":"SystemPrompt::Function(Arc::new(|pc: PromptContext| Box::pin(async move { Ok(Some(text)) }))); pc has session (user_id, org_id, meta), mode and task"},"2201":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-66","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#functions-are-closures-that-return-futures","content":"hooks.beforeModel, beforeTool, afterTool, onOutput"},"2202":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-67","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#functions-are-closures-that-return-futures","content":"fields of AgentHooks; each returns Ok(Some(result)) (BeforeToolResult { block: Some(why), .. }) or Ok(None) for no change"},"2203":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-68","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#functions-are-closures-that-return-futures","content":"approvals.policy"},"2204":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-69","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#functions-are-closures-that-return-futures","content":"Arc::new(|tool: PolicyTool, session: PolicySessionContext| Box::pin(async move { Ok(Some(ToolPolicy::Deny)) })); Ok(None) falls through"},"2205":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-70","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#functions-are-closures-that-return-futures","content":"onApproval, onElicitation (run or send options)"},"2206":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-71","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#functions-are-closures-that-return-futures","content":"RunOptions.on_approval, RunOptions.on_elicitation, which also get the run's CancellationToken"},"2207":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-72","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#errors-cancellation-and-closing","content":"Errors are returned, not thrown. Every fallible call returns Result<_, AgentError>. Each variant carries the failing part's error, so a caller can match on it: Config (validation), Loop (LoopError::Budget, an abort, a provider or structured-output failure), Provider, Workflow, Memory, Rag, Mcp, Other (your callback or store) and Message (TypeScript's plain messages, such as Session cancelled). A runtime that fails to build is cached as TypeScript caches the rejected promise: later calls return AgentError::Init around the same error, and err.root() unwraps it."},"2208":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-73","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#errors-cancellation-and-closing","content":"A panic is contained where TypeScript catches a throw. A panic in a tool body becomes a tool error the model reads; one in an event handler is reported on the error event."},"2209":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-74","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#errors-cancellation-and-closing","content":"Cancellation is a CancellationToken (tokio-util). Pass one in RunOptions.cancel where TypeScript passes an AbortSignal; a tool body gets a token that fires with the run or the tool's timeout."},"2210":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-75","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#errors-cancellation-and-closing","content":"Always agent.close().await, which disconnects MCP servers and closes memory and cache stores. A client Session has close(), which returns at once (safe inside an event handler), and shutdown().await, which also waits for the stream's task; dropping the Session closes its stream too."},"2211":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-76","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#errors-cancellation-and-closing","content":"Everything is Send + Sync: an Agent is cheap to clone and one agent serves many sessions from many tasks."},"2212":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-77","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"Results are JSON. result.output, tool results and wire payloads are serde_json::Value, because the engine passes them through as TypeScript does; decode them into your types at the edge."},"2213":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-78","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"define_tool returns Arc<ToolDef> while Config.tools holds ToolDef: unwrap with Arc::unwrap_or_clone."},"2214":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-79","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"JavaScript semantics where they show. String lengths in UTF-16 units, JavaScript's trim() and \\s, Number#toString, toFixed and Math.round are reproduced wherever their result reaches the wire, a prompt or a fixture, so output matches byte for byte."},"2215":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-80","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"Session ownership without AsyncLocalStorage. A session emits through an owned view of the agent's event bus, carried by each turn in a Tokio task-local, so the server routes subagent, RAG and MCP tool events to the session that raised them. A component that spawns its own task keeps the view with events::spawn_with_bus."},"2216":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-81","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"mcp::expose holds the agent weakly: the server stops when the agent is dropped (TypeScript and Go keep it alive until close), and it starts only on a running Tokio runtime."},"2217":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-82","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"Heavy drivers are Cargo features, as listed in Getting started."},"2218":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-83","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"The server is axum, and the handler has .router() and .close(). See One wire, four engines."},"2219":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-84","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"Rust-only additions: the tracing sink (feature tracing) and TelemetryConfig.extra_sinks, which runs it next to the collector."},"2220":{"id":"/docs/rust/config-reference-85","page_id":"/docs/rust/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust/config-reference#feature-status","content":"All of @agentkit/core, @agentkit/runtime, @agentkit/kernel, @agentkit/encoding, @agentkit/workspace, @agentkit/server and @agentkit/client (minus browser-only UI stores) are ported. The file-by-file checklist is Appendix A of docs/plans/python-go-sdk-port.md; sdks/rust/README.md has the phase table and the development commands."},"2221":{"id":"/docs/rust","page_id":"/docs/rust","type":"page","content":"Getting started (Rust)","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Rust"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/rust"},"2222":{"id":"/docs/rust-0","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust","content":"Add the crate and run your first agent in Rust"},"2223":{"id":"/docs/rust-1","page_id":"/docs/rust","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rust#getting-started-with-rust","content":"Getting started with Rust"},"2224":{"id":"/docs/rust-2","page_id":"/docs/rust","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rust#install","content":"Install"},"2225":{"id":"/docs/rust-3","page_id":"/docs/rust","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rust#your-first-agent","content":"Your first agent"},"2226":{"id":"/docs/rust-4","page_id":"/docs/rust","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rust#the-four-shapes","content":"The four shapes"},"2227":{"id":"/docs/rust-5","page_id":"/docs/rust","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rust#mock-mode-no-keys","content":"Mock mode, no keys"},"2228":{"id":"/docs/rust-6","page_id":"/docs/rust","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/rust#where-next","content":"Where next"},"2229":{"id":"/docs/rust-7","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#getting-started-with-rust","content":"sdks/rust is a full port of the AgentKit engine, not a client wrapper: providers, tools, memory, MCP, RAG, workflows, approvals, the plugin kernel, the workspace, the server and the client all run in your process, on Tokio. TypeScript stays the reference; shared fixtures and a client contract suite check that the four engines behave the same."},"2230":{"id":"/docs/rust-8","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#getting-started-with-rust","content":"The crate is published as headless-agentkit and imported as agentkit (the crate named agentkit on crates.io is an unrelated project). Releases are tagged sdks/rust/vX.Y.Z; the version tracks @agentkit/core's."},"2231":{"id":"/docs/rust-9","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#install","content":"Rust 1.88 or newer (edition 2024)."},"2232":{"id":"/docs/rust-10","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#install","content":"The default build runs the mock provider, the in-memory stores and SQLite (bundled, no system library). Everything else is a Cargo feature, so a program that never asks for a backend does not link its driver:"},"2233":{"id":"/docs/rust-11","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#install","content":"Feature"},"2234":{"id":"/docs/rust-12","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#install","content":"Brings"},"2235":{"id":"/docs/rust-13","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#install","content":"For"},"2236":{"id":"/docs/rust-14","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#install","content":"sqlite (default)"},"2237":{"id":"/docs/rust-15","page_id":"/do