":{"id":"/docs/rust-44","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#install","content":"Providers are raw HTTP over one reqwest client with rustls, so no vendor SDK or system OpenSSL is needed."},"2267":{"id":"/docs/rust-45","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#your-first-agent","content":"Every call that does I/O is async, and every fallible call returns Result<_, AgentError> where TypeScript throws."},"2268":{"id":"/docs/rust-46","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#your-first-agent","content":"Set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (or another provider's key). The config is a typed struct whose fields follow the TypeScript keys in snake_case; see Config in Rust."},"2269":{"id":"/docs/rust-47","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#the-four-shapes","content":"The README's four createAgent shapes, in Rust. Each runs on the mock provider in sdks/rust/tests/agent/readme_shapes.rs. The snippets below are function bodies with an agent agent in scope, as in the program above."},"2270":{"id":"/docs/rust-48","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#the-four-shapes","content":"A: backend task in, typed result out."},"2271":{"id":"/docs/rust-49","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#the-four-shapes","content":"B: full UI agent. The agent runs behind the AG-UI server (feature server); any frontend connects, including the TypeScript @agentkit/client and the React hooks."},"2272":{"id":"/docs/rust-50","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#the-four-shapes","content":"And from Rust (feature client):"},"2273":{"id":"/docs/rust-51","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#the-four-shapes","content":"C: backend with progress and approvals."},"2274":{"id":"/docs/rust-52","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#the-four-shapes","content":"D: terminal coding agent (feature workspace)."},"2275":{"id":"/docs/rust-53","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#mock-mode-no-keys","content":"test.mock_script (TypeScript's __test.mockScript) replaces the provider with a scripted one, for tests and CI:"},"2276":{"id":"/docs/rust-54","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#mock-mode-no-keys","content":"Every example in sdks/rust/examples runs with AGENTKIT_DEMO=mock and no API key:"},"2277":{"id":"/docs/rust-55","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#mock-mode-no-keys","content":"Example"},"2278":{"id":"/docs/rust-56","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#mock-mode-no-keys","content":"What it shows"},"2279":{"id":"/docs/rust-57","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#mock-mode-no-keys","content":"Features"},"2280":{"id":"/docs/rust-58","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#mock-mode-no-keys","content":"backend"},"2281":{"id":"/docs/rust-59","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#mock-mode-no-keys","content":"A: a backend task with tools and a typed result"},"2282":{"id":"/docs/rust-60","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#mock-mode-no-keys","content":"workspace"},"2283":{"id":"/docs/rust-61","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#mock-mode-no-keys","content":"http_api"},"2284":{"id":"/docs/rust-62","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#mock-mode-no-keys","content":"B: the agent's router nested in an axum app, serving the TypeScript page"},"2285":{"id":"/docs/rust-63","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#mock-mode-no-keys","content":"server"},"2286":{"id":"/docs/rust-64","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/rust#mock-mode-no-keys","content":"cli_agent"},"2287":{"id":"/docs/rust-65","page_id":"/docs/rust","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs