:"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#python-names-are-snake_case","content":"createCodingAgentPreset({ root, provider })"},"2395":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-34","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#python-names-are-snake_case","content":"create_coding_agent_preset(root=..., provider=...)"},"2396":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-35","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#python-names-are-snake_case","content":"Option and result objects are dataclasses with snake_case fields: RunResult (output, usage, trace, cost, step_count, tool_calls, trace_id, handoff), SQLConnectorConfig(dialect=, path=, max_rows=), ModelProviderConfig(id=, provider=, model=) for agent.models.add, HttpToolDef, ApiEndpointDef."},"2397":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-36","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#what-is-sent-stored-or-emitted-keeps-typescripts-keys","content":"Event payloads, wire bodies, recordings, session logs and anything persisted stay in TypeScript's shape, as dicts:"},"2398":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-37","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#what-is-sent-stored-or-emitted-keeps-typescripts-keys","content":"That is what lets a TypeScript UI read a Python server, and a log or recording written by one engine load in the other. Their types are TypedDicts in agentkit.types.events, so a type checker still sees the keys. agent.capabilities() returns the TypeScript keys too."},"2399":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-38","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#schemas-are-pydantic-models","content":"Where TypeScript takes a Zod schema, Python takes a pydantic model:"},"2400":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-39","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#schemas-are-pydantic-models","content":"execute receives a validated model instance. A structured output comes back as a model instance; use model_dump() for the dict."},"2401":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-40","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#functions-are-callables-and-may-be-async","content":"Every function-valued key takes a Python callable, sync or async:"},"2402":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-41","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#functions-are-callables-and-may-be-async","content":"Key"},"2403":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-42","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#functions-are-callables-and-may-be-async","content":"Python"},"2404":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-43","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#functions-are-callables-and-may-be-async","content":"system"},"2405":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-44","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#functions-are-callables-and-may-be-async","content":"def system(ctx) -> str, where ctx is a PromptContext (user_id, org_id, meta, mode, task)"},"2406":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-45","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#functions-are-callables-and-may-be-async","content":"hooks.beforeModel, beforeTool, afterTool, onOutput"},"2407":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-46","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#functions-are-callables-and-may-be-async","content":"receive a context dataclass (ctx.messages, ctx.name, ctx.args, ctx.result, 