on_approval=, on_elicitation="},"2416":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-55","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#functions-are-callables-and-may-be-async","content":"Configured plugins are Plugin dataclasses (Plugin(id=\"audit\", on_event=fn)); the field is id where TypeScript says name. Custom providers register with register_provider(id, factory), where the factory takes the optional API key from the config: def factory(api_key=None) -> Provider."},"2417":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-56","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#everything-that-does-io-is-async","content":"run, send, close, the models / rag / mcp / workflows APIs, serve and every client verb are coroutines. Event handlers are plain callables. Cancellation is a CancelSignal (run(..., signal=)) where TypeScript takes an AbortSignal. Always await agent.close(), which disconnects MCP servers and closes memory and cache stores."},"2418":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-57","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"Code Mode programs are Python. python_code_runtime runs them in a separate python -I process with an empty environment, over the same JSON-lines tool RPC; the host refuses programs that import, name a dunder or touch frame attributes. TypeScript's node:vm runtime has no Python counterpart."},"2419":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-58","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"JavaScript semantics where they show. Compact JSON.stringify output, JavaScript number formatting (5.0 as 5, 1e+21), String(), encodeURIComponent and toFixed rounding are reproduced wherever their result reaches the wire, a prompt or a fixture, so output matches byte for byte."},"2420":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-59","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"SQL connectors are production pools. MySQL runs on an aiomysql pool and streams results; Postgres runs on a psycopg pool, sends parameters as untyped text as pg does, keeps prepared statements off so PgBouncer works, and counts rows past maxRows on the server with a cursor. rowCount stays the total, as in TypeScript."},"2421":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-60","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"SQLite stores close cleanly. Each SQLite-backed store closes its connection when closed, dropped or at exit, and works as a context manager."},"2422":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-61","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"The server is ASGI. agentkit.server is one framework-free ASGI app; serve runs it on uvicorn. See One wire, four engines."},"2423":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-62","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#where-the-port-differs-and-why","content":"The client is async only. agentkit.client replaced the stdlib scaffold that lived in clients/python."},"2424":{"id":"/docs/python/config-reference-63","page_id":"/docs/python/config-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/config-reference#feature-status","content":"All of @agentkit/core, @agentkit/runtime, @agentkit/kernel, @agentkit/encoding, @agentkit/workspace, @agentkit/server and @agentkit/client (minus browser-only UI stores) are ported. The file-by-file checklist is Appendix A of docs/plans/python-go-sdk-port.md; sdks/python/README.md has the module table."},"2425":{"id":"/docs/python","page_id":"/docs/python","type":"page","content":"Getting started (Python)","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Python"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/python"},"2426":{"id":"/docs/python-0","page_id":"/docs/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python","content":"Install headless-agentkit and run your first agent in Python"},"2427":{"id":"/docs/python-1","page_id":"/docs/python","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/python#getting-started-with-python","content":"Getting started with Python"},"2428":{"id":"/docs/python-2","page_id":"/docs/python","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/python#install","content":"Install"},"2429":{"id":"/docs/python-3","page_id":"/docs/python","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/python#your-first-agent","content":"Your first agent"},"2430":{"id":"/docs/python-4","page_id":"/docs/python","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/python#the-four-shapes","content":"The four shapes"},"2431":{"id":"/docs/python-5","page_id":"/docs/python","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/python#mock-mode-no-keys","content":"Mock mode, no keys"},"2432":{"id":"/docs/python-6","page_id":"/docs/python","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/python#where-next","content":"Where next"},"2433":{"id":"/docs/python-7","page_id":"/docs/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python#getting-started-with-python","content":"sdks/python is a full port of the AgentKit engine, not a client wrapper: providers, tools, memory, MCP, RAG, workflows, approvals, the plugin kernel, the server and the client all run in your Python process. TypeScript stays the reference; shared fixtures and a client contract suite check that all four engines (TypeScript, Python, Go and Rust) behave the same."},"2434":{"id":"/docs/python-8","page_id":"/docs/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python#getting-started-with-python","content":"It is published on PyPI as headless-agentkit and imported as agentkit. The PyPI name agentkit belongs to an unrelated project."},"2435":{"id":"/docs/python-9","page_id":"/docs/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python#install","content":"Python 3.12 or newer."},"2436":{"id":"/docs/python-10","page_id":"/docs/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python#install","content":"Extra"},"2437":{"id":"/docs/python-11","page_id":"/docs/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python#install","content":"Brings"},"2438":{"id":"/docs/python-12","page_id":"/docs/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python#install","content":"For"},"2439":{"id":"/docs/python-13","page_id":"/docs/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python#install","content":"server"},"2440":{"id":"/docs/python-14","page_id":"/docs/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python#install","content":"uvicorn"},"2441":{"id":"/docs/python-15","page_id":"/docs/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python#install","content":"agentkit.server.serve"},"2442":{"id":"/docs/python-16","page_id":"/docs/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python#install","content":"mcp"},"2443":{"id":"/docs/python-17","page_id":"/docs/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python#install","content":"the official MCP SDK"},"2444":{"id":"/docs/python-18","page_id":"/docs/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python#install","content":"stdio and HTTP MCP servers"},"2445":{"id":"/docs/python-19","page_id":"/docs/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python#install","content":"postgres"},"2446":{"id":"/docs/python-20","page_id":"/docs/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python#install","content":"psycopg, psycopg-pool"},"2447":{"id":"/docs/python-21","page_id":"/docs/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python#install","content":"Postgres memory, the SQL connector"},"2448":{"id":"/docs/python-22","page_id":"/docs/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python#install","content":"mysql"},"2449":{"id":"/docs/python-23","page_id":"/docs/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python#install","content":