":{"id":"/docs/python/wire-28","page_id":"/docs/python/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/wire#one-wire-four-engines","content":"yes"},"2519":{"id":"/docs/python/wire-29","page_id":"/docs/python/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/wire#one-wire-four-engines","content":"yes"},"2520":{"id":"/docs/python/wire-30","page_id":"/docs/python/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/wire#one-wire-four-engines","content":"yes"},"2521":{"id":"/docs/python/wire-31","page_id":"/docs/python/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/wire#one-wire-four-engines","content":"agentkit::client (Rust)"},"2522":{"id":"/docs/python/wire-32","page_id":"/docs/python/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/wire#one-wire-four-engines","content":"yes"},"2523":{"id":"/docs/python/wire-33","page_id":"/docs/python/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/wire#one-wire-four-engines","content":"yes"},"2524":{"id":"/docs/python/wire-34","page_id":"/docs/python/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/wire#one-wire-four-engines","content":"yes"},"2525":{"id":"/docs/python/wire-35","page_id":"/docs/python/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/wire#one-wire-four-engines","content":"yes"},"2526":{"id":"/docs/python/wire-36","page_id":"/docs/python/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/wire#the-python-server","content":"agentkit.server is one framework-free ASGI app. serve runs it on uvicorn (extra server):"},"2527":{"id":"/docs/python/wire-37","page_id":"/docs/python/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/wire#the-python-server","content":"Inside another ASGI app, create_agent_handler(agent, base_path=\"/api/agent\", app=other_app) answers its routes and hands any other path to app. The routes are the TypeScript list: POST /session, GET /events (SSE, with Last-Event-ID replay), GET /events/all, POST /send, /approve, /reject, /answer, /cancel, GET /approvals, /history, /artifacts, GET|POST /mode, /workflows*, /mcp* (with the OAuth callback), /rag/*, /models*, /health, /capabilities. With transport=\"websocket\", /events is a WebSocket through the ASGI websocket scope. Auth, tenant isolation, CORS, Host checks, the 4 MiB body limit and the session cap are ported from handler.ts."},"2528":{"id":"/docs/python/wire-38","page_id":"/docs/python/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/wire#the-python-client","content":"agentkit.client talks to any AgentKit server:"},"2529":{"id":"/docs/python/wire-39","page_id":"/docs/python/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/wire#the-python-client","content":"It reconnects dropped streams, connect_with_retry waits for a server that is still starting, and connect_agents(url) talks to serve_agents. The session hub folds events with the same reducers as the TypeScript client (conversation, pending, todos, usage, workflow). The event stream starts with the first subscriber; wait for session.status == \"open\" (or hub.status) before a send whose events you must not miss."},"2530":{"id":"/docs/python/wire-40","page_id":"/docs/python/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/wire#how-the-sameness-is-checked","content":"The client contract, in all sixteen pairings. A contract host in each language (sdks/conformance/contract/ts_host.mjs, python_host.py, the Go one in sdks/go/internal/contracthost and the Rust examples/contract_host.rs) builds an agent from a JSON config and serves it on a free port (POST /serve, /serve-agents, /close). TypeScript's own packages/server/src/client-contract.test.ts runs unmodified against a host (a vitest setup redirects createAgent and serve to it), and its Python port sdks/python/tests/server/test_client_contract.py does the same, as do the Go and Rust ports:"},"2531":{"id":"/docs/python/wire-41","page_id":"/docs/python/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/wire#how-the-sameness-is-checked","content":"The wire frames, byte for byte. sdks/conformance/fixtures/wire.json holds the AG-UI frames the TypeScript adapter produces for every event name; the Python server replays them exactly. CI regenerates every fixture from the TypeScript source and fails on any difference."},"2532":{"id":"/docs/python/wire-42","page_id":"/docs/python/wire","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/python/wire#how-the-sameness-is-checked","content":"The dashboards, unchanged. Two pages built for the TypeScript server run against the Python one (and the Go and Rust ones) with no edits:"},"2533":{"id":"/docs/ui/client","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","type":"page","content":"Client","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","UI"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/ui/client"},"2534":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client","content":"@agentkit/client over AG-UI"},"2535":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ui/client#session-api","content":"Session API"},"2536":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ui/client#several-agents-several-sessions","content":"Several agents, several sessions"},"2537":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"Session hub"},"2538":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"UI state"},"2539":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ui/client#plain-html","content":"Plain HTML"},"2540":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client","content":"Framework-agnostic browser/Node connector. Handles session creation, the SSE event stream (with auto-reconnect), every REST action the server exposes, and pure reducers that turn events into UI state. It has no dependencies and no Node-only code. When the server uses transport: \"websocket\", connect with a WebSocket client to /events?sessionId=... instead."},"2541":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client","content":"The stream opens on the first on / onAny / onStatus and re-opens with exponential backoff when it drops. 401 / 403 are final: the status goes to closed with the error."},"2542":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client","content":"connect() itself fails at once when the server is down. When a page may load before its server, use connectWithRetry(url, { ...options, onRetry?, signal? }): it keeps trying while the server is unreachable (status 0) or answers 5xx, with the same backoff (reconnect; false disables), calls onRetry(error, attempt) before each new attempt, stops when signal aborts, and fails at once on any other answer (401, 404…). The React, Vue and Svelte useAgentSession use it."},"2543":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client","content":"In the browser the base URL may be a same-origin path (connect(\"/api/agent\"), e.g. a Next.js route using toFetchHandler); it resolves against the page."},"2544":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-api","content":"Method"},"2545":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-api","content":"Route"},"2546":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-api","content":"send(input, { mode?, model?, tools?, budget?, meta? })"},"2547":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-api","content":"POST /send — options apply to this run only"},"2548":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session