/ .remove(id) / .completeAuth(id, code)"},"2571":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-37","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-api","content":"GET /mcp, GET /mcp/:id/tools, POST /mcp/*"},"2572":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-api","content":"rag.sources() / .ingest(docs) / .query(q, k?)"},"2573":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-39","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-api","content":"/rag/* (ingest posts { docs })"},"2574":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-40","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-api","content":"models.list() / .setDefault(id) / .test(id) / .add(cfg) / .refresh() / .remove(id) / .usage()"},"2575":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-41","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-api","content":"/models/*"},"2576":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-42","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-api","content":"Every call checks the response and throws AgentKitError { status, message, body } on failure."},"2577":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-43","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"createSessionHub(url, options?) does that routing for you: one /events/all stream, every event folded into its session's state with the reducers below, so sessions in the background keep updating while the UI shows another."},"2578":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-44","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"Member"},"2579":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-45","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"session(id)"},"2580":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-46","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"A ClientSession for id (the same object per id): every call carries id, on / onAny see that session's events plus agent-wide ones (MCP, models) from the shared stream, send / answer emit client:send / client:answer, workflows.run closes the run in the hub's state when it returns. Pass it to any store or hook. Its close() detaches its listeners only"},"2581":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-47","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"state(id)"},"2582":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-48","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"{ conversation, pending, workflow, plan, todos, usage }; emptySessionState for a session it hasn't seen"},"2583":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-49","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"sessions() / subscribe(fn)"},"2584":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-50","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"Ids it knows (from events, session(), seed(), create()), in order; fn runs after any change"},"2585":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-51","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"seed(id) / create() / forget(id)"},"2586":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-52","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"Load history; start a session; drop one's state"},"2587":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-53","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"status / onStatus(fn) / close()"},"2588":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-54","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"The shared stream"},"2589":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-55","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#session-hub","content":"options are connect()'s (token, tenant, reconnect) plus conversation (passed to reduceConversation, e.g. { includeNested: true }). The hub loads the saved workflows (GET /workflows) on each (re)connect so a run shows every step up front."},"2590":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-56","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"Pure reducers turn the event stream into the state a UI renders. They are (state, event) => state, so they work in any framework, in tests and in a plain <script type=\"module\">."},"2591":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-57","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"Reducer"},"2592":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-58","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"State"},"2593":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-59","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"reduceConversation"},"2594":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-60","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"{ messages: [{ id, role, text, thinking?, tools, artifacts, parts, status, error? }], streaming } (status: streaming / done / stopped / error; stopped when the run was stopped, from done with status: \"stopped\") — parts interleave text, thinking, tool calls and questions (with the user's answer, from the local client:answer event); workflow-step and subagent events (scope) are left out unless { includeNested: true }"},"2595":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-61","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"reducePending"},"2596":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-62","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"{ approvals, questions } — cleared by approval:resolved / elicitation:resolved, the gated tool's result, and run end"},"2597":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-63","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"reduceWorkflowRun"},"2598":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-64","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"{ runs: [{ runId, workflowId, name, graph?, steps: [{ id, kind, label, tool?, input?, prompt?, status, output? }], status, output?, error? }], generating?, savePrompt? }"},"2599":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-65","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"reduceUsage"},"2600":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-66","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"{ tokens, inputTokens, outputTokens, cost, history } — cumulative across plan steps and subagents"},"2601":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-67","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"reduceMcp"},"2602":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-68","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"{ servers, tools }"},"2603":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-69","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"reduceEventLog"},"2604":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-70","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"{ rows: [{ id, at, phase, type, summary, payload, count? }] } — tokens merged, human summaries; groupByPhase(rows)"},"2605":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-71","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"reduceTodos / reducePlan"},"2606":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-72","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"{ todos } / { plan? }"},"2607":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-73","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"Session stores pair a reducer with its actions and keep it in sync while subscribed. Their subscribe matches the Svelte store contract."},"2608":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-74","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"A store takes a ClientSession (from connect() or hub.session(id)) or a bare event source ({ onAny }, e.g. streamAll()): without a session the state follows the events and the actions reject with \"Session not connected\"."},"2609":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-75","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#ui-state","content":"Also available: workflowRunStore (run, generate, save, dismissSavePrompt), workflowsStore (refresh, load, remove, save), mcpStore (server actions), usageStore, eventLogStore, todosStore (edit), planStore, and createStore(feed, reducer, initial) for your own reducers."},"2610":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-76","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#plain-html","content":"The package ships a dependency-free ES module build, so no bundler is needed:"},"2611":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-77","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#plain-html","content":"Do not import @agentkit/core in the browser. Run the agent on the server (serve() from @agentkit/server)."},"2612":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-78","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#plain-html","content":"Full protocol, endpoints, and vanilla JS: Streaming & wire protocol."},"2613":{"id":"/docs/ui/client-79","page_id":"/docs/ui/client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/client#plain-html","content":"Model switching parity: Models & switching."},"2614":{"id":"/docs/ui/custom","page_id":"/docs/ui/custom","type":"page","content":"Custom UI","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","UI"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/ui/custom"},"2615":{"id":"/docs/ui/custom-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/custom","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/custom","content":"Build from events without framework lock-in"},"2616":{"id":"/docs/ui/custom-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/custom","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/custom","content":"Any stack can consume the AG-UI wire:"},"2617":{"id":"/docs/ui/custom-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/custom","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/custom","content":"Vanilla — @agentkit/client from a module script (examples/express-api/public/index.html), or raw fetch + EventSource"},"2618":{"id":"/docs/ui/custom-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/custom","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/custom","content":"@agentkit/client — typed connect() + session.on(), reducers and stores"},"2619":{"id":"/docs/ui/custom-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/custom","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/custom","content":"React / Vue / Svelte — thin hooks over the same client"},"2620":{"id":"/docs/ui/custom-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/custom","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/custom","content":"Third-party AG-UI consumers — same event envelope { type, payload, timestamp }"},"2621":{"id":"/docs/ui/custom-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/custom","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/custom","content":"Design tips:"},"2622":{"id":"/docs/ui/custom-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/custom","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/custom","content":"Treat events as the source of truth; avoid polling /send for partial text."},"2623":{"id":"/docs/ui/custom-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/custom","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/custom","content":"Keep one SSE connection per UI session; multiplex handlers with session.on(type, fn)."},"2624":{"id":"/docs/ui/custom-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/custom","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/custom","content":"Approvals and elicitation are async: listen for approval:request / elicitation:request, then call the matching POST endpoints (or session.approve / answer)."},"2625":{"id":"/docs/ui/custom-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/custom","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/custom","content":"Point UI env vars at your server: NEXT_PUBLIC_AGENT_URL, VITE_AGENT_URL."},"2626":{"id":"/docs/ui/custom-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/custom","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/custom","content":"See Streaming & wire protocol for the full endpoint and event list."},"2627":{"id":"/docs/ui/react","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","type":"page","content":"React","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","UI"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/ui/react"},"2628":{"id":"/docs/ui/react-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/react","content":"@agentkit/react hooks and components"},"2629":{"id":"/docs/ui/react-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ui/react#hook-useagentsession","content":"Hook: useAgentSession"},"2630":{"id":"/docs/ui/react-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ui/react#state-hooks","content":"State hooks"},"2631":{"id":"/docs/ui/react-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ui/react#many-sessions-usesessionhub","content":"Many sessions: useSessionHub"},"2632":{"id":"/docs/ui/react-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ui/react#hook-usemodels","content":"Hook: useModels"},"2633":{"id":"/docs/ui/react-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/ui/react#components","content":"Components"},"2634":{"id":"/docs/ui/react-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/react#hook-useagentsession","content":"Connects on mount (same wire as @agentkit/client). Returns ready, client (the live session, as state), session (a ref to it), status (connecting / open / reconnecting / closed), error, on, send(input, options?), approve, reject, answer, cancel, saveWorkflow, and the last 200 events."},"2635":{"id":"/docs/ui/react-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/react#hook-useagentsession","content":"It reconnects only when the URL or the token / tenant / sessionId values change, so passing an inline options object is fine. When the server is down as the page loads, it keeps trying with the stream's backoff (reconnect), with status \"reconnecting\" and error set meanwhile (connectWithRetry from @agentkit/client); 4xx answers fail at once."},"2636":{"id":"/docs/ui/react-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/react#hook-useagentsession","content":"Register on() handlers only after ready === true. Unsubscribe in the useEffect cleanup."},"2637":{"id":"/docs/ui/react-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/react#state-hooks","content":"Most UIs don't need on() at all: pass client to a state hook and render what it returns. Each hook wraps a pure reducer from @agentkit/client, so the same logic runs in Vue, Svelte and plain JS."},"2638":{"id":"/docs/ui/react-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/react#state-hooks","content":"Hook"},"2639":{"id":"/docs/ui/react-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/react#state-hooks","content":"Returns"},"2640":{"id":"/docs/ui/react-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/react#state-hooks","content":"useConversation(client, { includeNested? })"},"2641":{"id":"/docs/ui/react-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/react#state-hooks","content":"{ messages, streaming } — each message has text, thinking?, tools, artifacts, ordered parts, status; workflow-step and subagent events stay out unless includeNested"},"2642":{"id":"/docs/ui/react-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/react#state-hooks","content":"usePendingRequests(client)"},"2643":{"id":"/docs/ui/react-15","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/react#state-hooks","content":"{ approvals, questions, approve, reject, answer } — a request disappears when it is settled anywhere (here, another tab, an admin console) or the run ends"},"2644":{"id":"/docs/ui/react-16","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/react#state-hooks","content":"useWorkflowRun(client)"},"2645":{"id":"/docs/ui/react-17","page_id":"/docs/ui/react","tags":[],"type":"text","u