 only from the plugin kernel"],[2482,"a coding agent built only from the plugin kernel"],[755,"A command that exits non-zero comes back with its exit code and output for the model, marked isError: true with the line that explains it (exited with code 1: Error: Cannot find module …), so it shows as a failed call in traces."],[1188,"A composition as data, so someone else can retune it without forking you"],[2920,"a computed list of audit rows"],[2924,"a computed plan"],[1701,"A config that fails to parse fails that plugin's fiber and leaves the rest of the tree running — one bad row does not take down the harness."],[1664,"A context with services"],[1636,"a ctx.credentials provider"],[1602,"a ctx.shell provider"],[1600,"a ctx.terminals backend + terminalTools"],[1610,"a ctx.web / ctx.lsp provider"],[2978,"a cycle, a bad id or an empty/oversized graph rejects the draft."],[1846,"A decision is { kind: \"allow\" }, { kind: \"deny\", reason }, or { kind: \"ask\", question }. The runtime — not your plugin — runs the tools/ask serial when a listener answers ask, so asking and answering stay independently replaceable."],[1386,"A deferred tool stays registered and callable, so ctx.tools.execute and\nCode Mode still reach it. What changes is ctx.tools.schemas()."],[1679,"A dependency here is a relationship over time, not a startup-order constraint. The plugin loads when its dependencies appear, unloads when one disappears, and reloads when it comes back."],[1267,"A grep matching four thousand lines is not a bug — the answer really is four thousand lines. Truncating throws away what the model needed; inlining costs the window. Spilling keeps the whole result addressable and returns a head plus a locator."],[1312,"A hook is not a plugin: it is a line of config pointing at a script. That is the whole point — \"run the formatter after every edit\" or \"never let it touch .env\" should not require writing TypeScript, publishing a package, or restarting anything."],[1173,"A job queue with retries and priority. ctx.jobs runs work in the background; a durable queue across restarts is a product choice (pg-boss, BullMQ, or a small table)."],[1198,"A later bundle re-declaring an id overrides that row in place rather than appending a duplicate, so extends composes without reordering surprises."],[1474,"A line of config can veto a tool"],[1271,"A loop lets the model choose the next action; a workflow fixes it in advance. Both are useful, and the mistake is making one pretend to be the other. Steps declare needs, so independent ones run concurrently without the author scheduling anything."],[1311,"A malformed settings file fails loudly at load. Silently ignoring it would mean a typo'd JSON file makes a policy quietly stop applying — the failure mode worth the least tolerance."],[1098,"A minimal v1"],[1725,"a mode changes the visible tool set and the prompt, per agent"],[1281,"A model that can only make one tool call per step spends a step filtering a list, another chaining a result into the next call, and a third summarising. Code Mode collapses that: every visible tool becomes await tools.<name>(args) inside a single run_code program."],[1101,"A multi-session coding agent runs in a terminal, a desktop shell or a web chat without owning an editor. It keeps many conversations, each with its own history and workspace; reads, edits, greps and runs commands in a project root behind approvals and a sandbox; delegates to subagents; persists sessions across restarts and reconnects clients to work in flight."],[1534,"A narrower world for one agent"],[1243,"A one-shot shell loses everything between calls: a cd, an activated virtualenv, an SSH session, a REPL. That is the right default — reproducible and cheap — which is exactly why the stateful case needs its own seam rather than a flag on the stateless one."],[2208,"A panic is contained where TypeScript catches a throw. A panic in a tool body becomes a tool error the model reads; one in an event handler is re