t for that shape at the plugin level, not the config level. createAgent and @agentkit/workspace still work for the simple case, but a product like this is a harness, and the spine is where a harness lives: createRuntime, agentRuntime(), and plugins on public extension points. Two examples prove it and are the right starting points:"],[418,"AgentKit ships a single-file guide written for AI coding assistants: every feature, the full config, events, the server/client/hook APIs and recipes. Install it into your project and your assistant builds with the SDK instead of hand-rolling servers, reconnects or approval queues:"],[628,"AgentKit Studio (studio)"],[825,"AgentKit surfaces runtime activity as typed AG-UI events rather than only stdout. Set logging.level to control log emissions from the agent shell, and subscribe to cost:update for per-turn token and cost estimates from the active provider."],[595,"AgentKit uses config over code at every level:"],[2354,"agentkit::client (feature client) talks to any AgentKit server:"],[2119,"agentkit::client (Rust)"],[2344,"agentkit::client (Rust)"],[2521,"agentkit::client (Rust)"],[2262,"agentkit::client, for any AgentKit server"],[2174,"agentkit::create_agent(config) returning Result<Agent, AgentError>"],[2146,"agentkit::create_agent(config) takes an agentkit::Config. Each field is the TypeScript key in snake_case, nested blocks are their own structs (in agent::config or the module they configure), and every optional field is an Option. Config has no Default, because the provider is required: start from Config::new(provider) and use struct update syntax."],[2188,"agentkit::events::on(agent.bus(), keys::STREAM_TOKEN, fn) (typed) or agent.on(\"stream:token\", fn)"],[2349,"agentkit::server (feature server) is built on axum. serve binds a listener of its own and returns its URL and a close handle:"],[2259,"agentkit::server, the AG-UI routes"],[2109,"agentkit.client (Python)"],[2334,"agentkit.client (Python)"],[2511,"agentkit.client (