e question a layered config always has to answer at 2am, which is why explain() exists alongside get(). describe() lists the mounted layers; override() sets a value in a layer of its own, so a runtime change is visibly an override rather than an edit to somebody else's file."],[1883,"This is why the transcript UI in mini-harness imports no tool, and gets new tools' cards for free."],[2356,"Three things differ from TypeScript. Handlers for server events run on the task that reads the stream, so keep them short or hand work off. close() returns at once (a handler may call it) while shutdown().await also waits for that task. And dropping a Session closes its event stream, as dropping the last clone of a SessionHub closes the hub, so hold on to them while you listen. send waits for a stream that is still connecting, then returns once the handlers have seen the run's done."],[1283,"Three tool calls and a filter, in one step, one result."],[1084,"Throwing from execute fails the call, and the model gets the error message. When the model\nshould still see the whole result (a command's exit code and output, a partial response),\nreturn it with isError: true and an optional error. The model gets the full result, and the\ncall is recorded as failed: a red tool span with that error in traces, counted in the trace's\n\"N failed calls\" badge and found by the has:error filter."],[2673,"Timeline — ordered plan/workflow/tool steps (pass events from your session reducer)"],[1915,"title?, content?"],[1172,"Titles and metadata. A title, a cwd, a model label per session. Keep them in your own store keyed by session id, or log them as your own event type and project them."],[1242,"To confine commands by the operating system instead, mount sandboxedShell from @agentkit/workspace in place of localShell. Every command runs in root whatever cwd it asks for, can write only there (plus writableRoots), has no network unless network: true, and the system prompt tells the model so (prompt: false